{title: Oh! Susanna}
{artist: Stephen Foster}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 104}
{meta: public_domain Words and music by Stephen Foster, published 1848.}
{meta: source Foster's 1848 sheet music; dialect spelling modernised.}
{meta: arrangement Original chord arrangement for Fretlight. Only verses free of the original's period slurs are included.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I [G]come from Ala[G]bama with my [G]banjo on my [D]knee,
I'm [G]going to Louisi[G]ana, my [D]true love for to [G]see.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Oh! [C]Susanna, [C]oh, don't you [G]cry for [D]me,
For I [G]come from Ala[G]bama with my [D]banjo on my [G]knee.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
It [G]rained all night the [G]day I left, the [G]weather it was [D]dry,
The [G]sun so hot I [G]froze to death; Su[D]sanna, don't you [G]cry.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
